1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,622
Three charts. Three new skills to test.

2
00:00:02,991 --> 00:00:04,801
Breakouts, momentum and traps.

3
00:00:05,301 --> 00:00:08,299
Question one. Price just closed above resistance.

4
00:00:08,648 --> 00:00:10,104
Real breakout, or fake?

5
00:00:13,954 --> 00:00:14,516
Fake.

6
00:00:14,924 --> 00:00:21,789
The break came on thin volume, and price couldn't hold above the level. Real breakouts usually hold it on a retest.

7
00:00:22,289 --> 00:00:27,484
Question two. Price just made a new high. Now check the RSI panel underneath.

8
00:00:27,823 --> 00:00:29,523
Will this new high hold, or fail?

9
00:00:33,373 --> 00:00:34,077
It failed.

10
00:00:34,472 --> 00:00:42,757
Price made a higher high, but RSI made a lower one. That divergence showed momentum fading. It's a warning, not a certainty.

11
00:00:43,257 --> 00:00:46,005
Question three. Price just dipped below support.

12
00:00:46,379 --> 00:00:48,749
Is this a real breakdown, or a bear trap?

13
00:00:52,599 --> 00:00:53,411
A bear trap.

14
00:00:53,748 --> 00:01:00,843
The dip came on thin volume, then buyers snapped it straight back above support. Sellers who shorted the break got caught.

15
00:01:01,343 --> 00:01:04,087
How many did you get? Tell me your score in the comments.

16
00:01:04,478 --> 00:01:08,109
Practise on real charts from the game, at memestreet.net.

